19. But how many are there really?'--'Five,' he replied.--'Five, indeed,' he said; 'the sacrifice is fivefold; the sacrificial animal is fivefold [^egg_465]; there are five seasons in the year, and the sacrifice is the year;

[^egg_465]: 154:2 For the 'pāṅkta' nature of the sacrifice, see III, 1, 4, 19. 20; XIII, 2, 5, 1, for the five kinds of sacrificial animals, VI, 1, 2, 32 seqq.

and one and the same day are those two, the Caturviṁśa and the Mahāvrata.;--
